Infer an ``enum`` member whose integer value is past the int-to-str conversion
limit, such as ``A = 0xff...`` (a large hex literal the tokenizer accepts).
Rendering the value back in decimal for the mocked member class previously made
``infer_enum_class`` raise an uncaught ``ValueError`` while building the module;
the value is now rendered as a hex literal instead.

Refs #3256
